                <pb facs="0328" n="258" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg258"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">wishes.</hi></head>
                <p>The conference expresses the wish that the powers shall, as early as possible,
                    come to an understanding as to the signals which ships employed in laying or
                    repairing submarine cables shall have to make in order to remove all doubts as
                    to the nature of their operations.</p>
                <p>The conference also expresses the wish that the different Governments shall take
                    measures in order that the track of the submarine cables be indicated by beacons
                    placed on the shores, and that, after an international understanding, a uniform
                    type of beacons and of buoys be adopted for the submarine telegraphic
                    service.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
